      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZWICK (5) scored an all of the way win two runs back at Terang from a nice gate. Drew a wide gate last start and was easily accounted for, beaten 1.5 metres into fourth at Melton over 1720m. Won't find this any harder and he can bounce back straight away. HURRICANE HOOLY (4) settled in the leading division but didn't find enough in the end and could only manage ninth last start over 1720m at Melton, that effort coming after a minor placing at Cranbourne the run before. Her last run should be overlooked. Good enough to win a race of this calibre. AMERICAN SQUARED (3) is worth thought after finishing fourth first-up over 2190m at Maryborough last time out after he was checked in the running. KIMCHI (1) disappointed last time when sixth over 2190m at Maryborough afetr having led at the bell. Can do a lot better and from the inside draw is worth considering.",
